# College Chatbot Powered by Groq & ChromaDB

A smart chatbot that scrapes your college website, stores information using state-of-the-art embeddings and vector search, and answers questions with advanced AI models from Groq.

--------------------------------------------------------

## Project Overview

This project creates a question-answering chatbot interface for college information.
- Scrapes college website pages for facts and content
- Converts and stores the data in a searchable database
- Lets users query with natural language
- Fetches relevant context and uses Groq LLMs to generate clear answers

--------------------------------------------------------

## File Structure

scraper.py          | Scrapes HTML from college site & cleans visible text
ingest.py           | Splits text, embeds with sentence transformers, indexes in ChromaDB
app.py              | Runs chat frontend in Streamlit, retrieves context, calls LLM API
requirements.txt    | Contains required Python library versions (manage via conda & pip)
.env.example        | Template for env variables (API keys/model names)
.env                | Your actual secrets (should NOT be shared)

--------------------------------------------------------

## Setup Instructions

**Step 1: Create your Conda environment**
    conda create -n college-chatbot python=3.12 -y
    conda activate college-chatbot

**Step 2: Install dependencies**
    conda install -c conda-forge chromadb
    pip install -r requirements.txt

**Step 3: Set up environment variables**
    - Copy .env.example to .env
    - Add your actual Groq API key and select your Groq LLM model (from your available list)

Example .env:
    GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key
    LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

--------------------------------------------------------

## Usage Workflow

1. Edit scraper.py to set the main URL of your college website
2. Run:        python scraper.py
   (This fetches text data from the site)
3. Run:        python ingest.py
   (This embeds and indexes data in ChromaDB)
4. Start UI:   streamlit run app.py
   (Use the browser to chat and ask questions!)

--------------------------------------------------------

## Technical Stack Highlights

- requests and BeautifulSoup:      HTML page download & parsing for clean text
- lxml:                            Advanced/fast HTML parsing (if set in scraper)
- sentence-transformers:           Embedding text into semantic vector space
- ChromaDB:                        Efficient vector database for retrieval
- Streamlit:                       Lightweight, reactive UI for chatting
- Groq LLM API:                    Large language model backend for answer generation

--------------------------------------------------------

## Troubleshooting (“Lessons Learned”)

- If pip/conda have dependency issues, use conda for native packages and pip for standard Python libs.
- If chroma-hnswlib fails to build: remove from pip, use only conda for chromadb.
- If your LLM model is decommissioned/by Groq: use Groq API to list valid models and update your config.
- If API key issues: test with curl or Python requests to verify access.
- For VSCode, activate conda environment and ensure Python interpreter matches.

